    {
        "content": "<p>This is also in batteries: <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=instLawfulMonadIO_batteries#doc\">docs#instLawfulMonadIO_batteries</a>. Note that this also using the module system -- <code>import all</code> is your friend here.</p>",
        "id": 595416182,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1778888353
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also I think it's perfectly reasonable for IO to be lawful -- I don't think you can really call something a monad if it weren't lawful (except if it turned out the laws would be true but unprovable).</p>",
        "id": 595416303,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
